00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.710
today we're gonna do some titration calculations

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.490
consider the following acid-base
reaction we have hydrochloric acid and

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:20.939
sodium hydroxide yielding sodium
chloride and water if 50 milliliters of

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:26.490
an HCl solution with unknown
concentration are titrated with zero

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:32.610
point two five zero molar sodium
hydroxide and then if it takes 35 point

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.309
two three milliliters of base to reach
the equivalence point what was the

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:43.410
concentration of the HCL solution so if
you're not sure how to approach this go

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.540
ahead and check out my tutorial on
titration and when you're ready give it a try.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.500
so let's put our reaction up top and
then what we need to remember about the

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.810
equivalence point is that it is the
point where the moles of acid equals

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:21.900
moles of base so it is the point where
precisely all of the acid has been

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:27.270
neutralized by the base so it is telling
us something about stoichiometry when

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:31.829
the equivalence point is reached so
since we want to find out the moles of

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:37.710
acid let's find the moles of base so
let's take our volume of base we have

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.000
thirty five point two four milliliters
of base that were required to reach the

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.829
equivalence point and let's first
convert that into leaders so dividing by

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:52.140
a thousand milliliters we have 0.03 five
to four liters of Base to reach the

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.170
equivalence point now since we have the
concentration of that base we can

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.390
convert liters into moles so let's take
our liters of base and multiply by 0.25

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:10.410
zero multiplied not means that was zero
point zero zero eight eight one moles of

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:16.410
base that were required to reach the
point now we have to look at the

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.900
stoichiometric ratio the acid in the
base are in a one-to-one ratio so that

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:27.180
means if that many moles of base were
required to reach the equivalence point

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:32.130
then we multiply by one mole of acid
over one mole of base and we get that

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:38.250
same number of moles back for the acid
so when the equivalence point was

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:44.640
reached that many moles of base had
precisely neutralized that many moles of

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.980
acid and that is the number of moles of
acid that were in the solution initially

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.990
for the HCl solution so now all we have
to do is convert that many moles of acid

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:59.460
into a concentration and so
concentration is moles per liter so we

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:05.880
take our moles of acid and we divide by
0.0500 liters because we know we had

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.020
fifty point zero milliliters of acid we
knew the volume we just didn't know the

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:16.710
concentration so that many moles over
that many liters gives us 0.176 moles

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:24.860
per liter or point 176 molar HCl which
was the concentration of our unknown HCl solution.

